Subject: net: phylink: pass physical media to PCS configuration (OpenWrt realtek 744, forward-ported to v7.4-rc3)

OpenWrt main (2026-10-26, Jonas Jelonek, realtek/patches-6.18/744) extends the phylink PCS API: pcs_config() takes
a struct phylink_media (physical medium, passive cable length, attachment generation) and phylink delivers
media-none on removal/detach. The rewritten pcs-rtl-otto.c needs it (media_teardown, the new pcs_config signature).
- Forward-port: the phylink.c / phylink.h hunks apply to v7.4-rc3 with fuzz 2-3 (regenerated here, exact context);
  driver callbacks adapted for the drivers that apply on rc3. Dropped (do not apply, not built in our configs):
  mxl862xx, macb, fbnic, pcs-mtk-lynxi, pcs-mtk-usxgmii.
- 7.x flows only (build_openwrt.py mainline, mainline_build_check.py); the 6.18 build already gets 744 from OpenWrt.
Signed-off-by: Jonas Jelonek <jonas@jonasjelonek.de>
---
